  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b3bd7e19cd35d3748afe2962d0eae4a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ChangelogScript
  VersionChanges:
  - Version: 2.0.0 beta 1.0
    VanillaVersionBase: 2.1.0.1
    MajorChanges:
    - the game now uses mvlo 2.0 as a base, this fixes MANY janky interactions and
      bugs, and comes with a couple new features such as the hammer suit
    - several maps/features were "removed" due to requireing more development time,
      these most likely WILL RETURN in future versions
    - reworked the gamerules customisation for advanced lobbies
    - ANYTHING can spawn as a powerup if you make it part of the *powerup list
    - ANYTHING can spawn as a hazard if you make it part of the *hazard list
    - added new characters (shy guy, toadette)
    - added boss hazards (bowser, petey piranha, king boo, whomp king)
    - added conversion cauldron, chainpost, baseball, billblock, cannonbox, tanoomba,
      fan, & starball hazards
    - non-hefty hazards also appear on the minimap
    - added drill joke powerup
    Changes:
    - added scale lifts, if you step on it it moves down and the other moves up
    - added dry bones, and big dry bones
    - added big thwomps
    - multi area maps now only show things on the minimap that are on your layer
    - improved model quality a bit
    - added more animations to some characters
    - bubbleflower bubbles now lightly explode when popped
    - bubbleflower bubbles that kill enemies properly store the coin in them now
    - bubbleflower bubbles can no longer capture a player
    - bubbleflower bubbles will now capture throwables and projectiles
    - bombro dropping a bomb will no longer make it walk, this allows you to place
      it down as a trap
    - bombro's groundpound explodes more blocks
    - bioflower can now pickup carryables
    - if you bioflower grapple anything that isn't a wall the grapple slows down
      a little bit
    - bioflower grappling a star no longer makes it go torwards you, instead you
      go torwards it
    - pocketdoor teleport is entierly reworked (again)
    - metalmushroom item uses a model
    - metalmushroom's top speed increases in speed everytime you land
    - jumpsuit now lets you triplejump anywhere, not just doublejump
    - supercrown no longer spawns naturally
    - doneflower doneballs will swap your powerup with whatever player you hit
    - goldblock is no longer a wearable, and is now a throwable. it keeps ALL of
      it's previous features otherwise
    - pows now linger for 10 extra frames, making them easier to hit (looking at
      you bluepow)
    - the propellerblock now changes color depending on the player, a trait shared
      by some new carryables
    - freezie now freezes your foes for longer making it more worth using
    - the voidwall is now a carryable, after thrown it creates the wall
    - bowsershell's speed has been increased, inflicts a different type of knockback
    - springboard & lemmyball hazards now interact with everything that moves
    - lemmyball no longer hops on liquids
    - 'several other changes to improve the experience '
  - Version: 1.2.1 (640.2.1) & bellow
    VanillaVersionBase: 1.7.1-1.7.1
    MajorChanges:
    - pre-1.7.1 changelogs are no longer supported, are in poor quality, and are
      quite old
    - you can view them in the archived versions if you insist on seeing them (insert
      link to archive)
    Changes:
    - e
